      "body": "## Motivation\r\n\r\nTorch-profiler triage of DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash at main `730f1f3e5b` on 4x B200 (cookbook TP4+EP4 low-latency cell, DSPARK block 5) shows the mHC mix-stats pair (`_hc_mix_stats_partial_kernel` + `_hc_mix_reduce_sinkhorn_kernel`) is the single largest decode kernel family: ~32% of decode GPU time at bs=1, ~86 calls per spec iteration (one per hc sublayer, 40 layers x attn/ffn + MTP).\r\n\r\n`_num_stages_for` enables `num_stages=1` only for `64 <= m <= 384`, so decode/verify row counts (M <= 8 at bs=1) fall through and launch the partial kernel with `num_stages=2`. At these sizes the extra pipeline stage only adds shared-memory footprint and scheduling overhead: the whole K loop is 4 x BLOCK_K=64 tiles per slice.\r\n\r\n## Modification\r\n\r\nDrop the lower bound of the `num_stages=1` window: `64 <= m <= 384` becomes `m <= 384` (Blackwell, K=20480 unchanged).\r\n\r\n`num_stages` only reorders memory issue, not arithmetic, so the partials are bitwise unchanged — verified with `torch.equal` on `part_mix`/`part_sq` against `num_stages=2` for M in {1, 7, 8, 64, 128}. Batch invariance (K slicing, BLOCK_K, dot precision, BLOCK_M buckets) is untouched. (For the record: `num_warps` is *not* a bit-safe knob — the `tl.sum(x*x)` reduction tree changes with warp count — so it stays at 4.)\r\n\r\n## Benchmarks\r\n\r\nKernel level, B200, K=20480 (hc_mult 4 x hidden 5120), CUDA-graph replay timings:\r\n\r\n| M | pair before (us) | pair after (us) | partial alone |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| 1 | 19.4 | 10.1 | — |\r\n| 7 | 22.2 | 13.2 (-41%) | 14.2 -> 5.0 |\r\n| 8 | 22.7 | 13.6 | — |\r\n| 64 | 54.9 | 20.6 (-62%) | — |\r\n\r\nEnd to end, DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash on 4x B200 (TP4+EP4, `--speculative-algorithm DSPARK --speculative-dspark-block-size 5 --cuda-graph-max-bs-decode 64`), 256K-token prompt, bs=1, out 512, same-seed pairs:\r\n\r\n| seed | decode before (tok/s) | decode after (tok/s) |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| 70 | 903 | 1138 (+26%) |\r\n| 72 | 890 | 1038 (+17%) |\r\n\r\nTTFT unchanged (4.87-4.88 s before and after): prefill row counts do not route through this backend (bf16x3/DeepGEMM paths), and 64 <= m <= 384 already had `num_stages=1`.\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [ ] Format your code: `pre-commit run --all-files` (not run locally — comment + one-condition diff; CI lint will confirm)\r\n- [x] Add unit tests: covered by existing mHC bitwise/batch-invariance tests; the change is launch-config only and bitwise verified above.\r\n- [x] Update documentation as needed: measurement recorded in the code comment.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37559928231](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37559928231)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #37560370708](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37560370708)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37559928194](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37559928194)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
